[Music]  are you ready for the uk  transition number two key dates and  stages  [Music]  my name is jane rose and i'm head of  international trade at the essex  chambers of commerce  this is the second of four bite size  videos about the uk transition  which have been commissioned by rochford  district council to help businesses  prepare for the changes to trading with  the eu  contact and website details are listed  in the video description  in this video i'm going to tell you  about the three stages that the  government have put in place  to give you more time to make the  changes you need ahead of the uk  transition  from the 1st of january 2021 all goods  leaving and arriving at the uk border  will need export and import declarations  this may be new to you so let me explain  a form called a c88 or sad  a single administrative document is used  to make the declaration to customs  this is then lodged with the uk customs  computer  which is called chief chief currently  logs all movement of goods  in and out of the uk outside of the eu  and from january the 1st that will  include all trade to and from the eu as  well  completing the declaration properly  requires a lot of information and  specialist knowledge  whether it's done by you or a third  party  you'll need to find out if your goods  need a licence or special certificates  for items such as animals or animal  products  plants and plant products you'll also  need to check  to see if your goods are listed as  controlled and there'll be extra checks  at the border for certain goods  if you're importing standard goods from  the eu which is everything from clothes  to electronics  you may be able to delay the import  declaration and duties for six months  but do consider the implications in  doing this as it will have to be done  eventually  now on to the second stage from the  first of april 2021  all products of animal origin such as  meat pet food honey  milk or egg products and all regulated  plants and plant products  will need to have import  pre-notifications submitted  and the relevant health certificate and  lastly  the third and final stage from the 1st  of july 2021  you'll need to meet full customs  requirements for all imports and exports  this means providing full important  safety and security  there'll be an increase in physical  checks and all import duties and vat  will need to be paid  this is a really big change for those of  you that have only been trading with the  eu up until now  i understand that it's a lot to take in  but i hope this has given you an idea of  what you need to be doing to prepare  please do contact us at the essex  chambers of commerce if you need  training or advice  on where to start and don't forget there  are web links and references listed in  the video description thank you so much  for listening

